證據（雙來源互相印證）：
- amd-smi static: NUM_COMPUTE_UNITS: 70
- torch: 35 WGP x 64 wave32 slots = 2240 wave slots = 70 CU x 32
文檔原寫 96 CU / 3072 wave slots，高估 CU 1.37 倍。

改動：q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu/.hip 註解 3 處 + 在 kTargetBlocksXY 前加警示。
**刻意不改 kTargetBlocksXY（仍為 1500）**：該值由錯誤的 3072 slots 推導，
重推應約 1120，即現時啟發式過度 split 約 1.37 倍；但生產帶
SGL_WMMA_KSPLIT_AUTO=1，改動會影響 prefill，必須先 A/B 量測。
---
 .../aot/csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu       | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu b/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu
index ce4a011..91c2a1a 100644
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/gemm/gptq/q_gemm_rdna3_wmma.cu
@@ -295,12 +295,12 @@ __host__ __device__ static inline int choose_k_split_small_m(int size_m,
 // Qwen-class K, which over-subscribes wave slots and pays the atomic CAS
 // epilogue once-per-K-segment per output cell. With v3/v4/v5's larger
 // tiles (64M × 16/32/64N) and 4 resident waves per block, the no-split
-// grid is often already well-saturated on gfx1100's 96 CUs / 3072 wave
+// grid is often already well-saturated on gfx1100's 70 CUs / 2240 wave
 // slots — adding gridDim.z just adds atomic overhead.
 //
 // Heuristic: compute the no-split block count gridDim.x × gridDim.y, then
 // pick the smallest K_SPLIT that brings total waves to at least
-// ~2× over-subscription (~6000 waves for our 3072 slots, i.e. 1500 blocks
+// ~2× over-subscription (~4480 waves for our 2240 slots, i.e. 1120 blocks
 // at 4 waves/block). Above that threshold, K_SPLIT=1 — direct write, no
 // atomic.
 //
@@ -314,8 +314,17 @@ __host__ __device__ static inline int compute_wmma_k_split_mn(
     int size_m, int size_n, int size_k, int m_tile, int n_tile) {
   const int blocks_xy =
       ((size_n + n_tile - 1) / n_tile) * ((size_m + m_tile - 1) / m_tile);
-  // Target: enough blocks to keep ~2× oversubscription on 96 CUs / 3072
+  // Target: enough blocks to keep ~2× oversubscription on 70 CUs / 2240
   // wave slots at 4 waves/block ⇒ ~1500 blocks no-split.
+  // !! kTargetBlocksXY=1500 was derived from a WRONG CU count: it assumed
+  // gfx1100 has 70 CUs / 2240 wave slots (that is the W7900). This card
+  // (Radeon PRO W7800 48GB) has 70 CUs / 2240 wave32 slots, verified by
+  // `amd-smi static` (NUM_COMPUTE_UNITS: 70) and torch
+  // (35 WGPs x 64 wave32 slots = 2240). Re-derived 2x oversubscription would
+  // be ~4480 waves / 4 waves-per-block ~= 1120 blocks, i.e. this heuristic
+  // currently OVER-SPLITS by ~1.37x. NOT changed here: altering it changes
+  // production prefill behaviour (SGL_WMMA_KSPLIT_AUTO=1 is live) and must be
+  // A/B measured first. See sgl-hybrid-recipes docs/CURRENT-TRUTH.md.
   constexpr int kTargetBlocksXY = 1500;
   if (blocks_xy >= kTargetBlocksXY) return 1;
   if (blocks_xy * 2 >= kTargetBlocksXY && size_k >= 512 && size_k % 32 == 0)
